; An index's line comes before the lines that rely on it: consult's line
; ran before the index was installed, so its import raised, saying the
; line has no source, and installed nothing.
! import: the line for consult has no source: give it a git or local clause, or use an index that names it (use-plugin consult) at line 2, char 1 of ~/.config/tuna/init.ss
> (memq 'consult (installed-plugins))
#f
> (installed-plugins)
(sources)
> (use-plugin magit)
! import: the line for magit has no source: give it a git or local clause, or use an index that names it
; Once the index is installed, its lines are known.
> (use-plugin consult)
> (consult:buffer)
"compat buffer"
; A plugin that holds no main module, or a missing commit, installs
; nothing.
> (install-plugin! '(use-plugin empty (git "https://github.com/bob/empty")))
! install-plugin!: plugin empty holds no module (empty)
> (use-plugin empty (git "https://github.com/bob/empty"))
! import: plugin empty holds no module (empty)
> (use-plugin vertico (git "https://github.com/minad/vertico") (commit "0000000"))
! import: commit 0000000 not found in https://github.com/minad/vertico
> (installed-plugins)
(consult sources compat)
